1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,440
Click 'Reject optional'. The banner goes away.

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:12,360
The simulated analytics module keeps sending: 4 requests in total.

3
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:18,190
Four parts: consent UI, preference store, analytics module, collector.

4
00:00:18,190 --> 00:00:25,310
The collector is local and simulated. No real service is contacted.

5
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:33,340
The buttons write the preference. Nothing executing ever reads it.

6
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:42,170
No cookie is needed for this: an in-memory ID is enough.

7
00:00:42,170 --> 00:00:49,590
A consent state machine drives one gate: open only in 'accepted'.

8
00:00:49,590 --> 00:00:59,030
init, track and flush each check the gate. Withdraw removes listeners, clears the queue.

9
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:06,090
No choice 0 · Rejected 0 · Reload with stored rejection 0.

10
00:01:06,090 --> 00:01:11,970
Accepted 3 · Withdraw: unsent event dropped, count stays 3.

11
00:01:11,970 --> 00:01:20,230
Flawed: 4 requests, 3 marked 'rejected'. Corrected: 3, all 'accepted'.

12
00:01:20,230 --> 00:01:27,660
Stopping future requests does not delete data already collected.

13
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:33,820
First-party does not mean necessary or exempt. Not a legal certification.

14
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:39,420
The button is a promise. The requests show the implementation.
